@startuml LaPrizzaDomainModel
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide methods

title Domain Model Excerpt - WEB01 SPA Setup and Integration (Business Identifiers)

' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' WEB01 introduces NO new domain concept.
' The excerpt shows the aggregates whose information the SPA reads and maintains
' ONLY through the Back-End API, and the identifiers that must stay consistent
' across the SPA, the 3D viewer (VIS) and the AI module (AC 3).
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

package "User Aggregate" <<Rectangle>> {

    class User <<entity>> <<aggregateRoot>> {
        + active : boolean
    }

    class UserId <<vo>> {
        + value : string
    }
    note right of UserId
        Example: "USR-00123".
    end note

    enum UserRole <<enum>> {
        ADMINISTRATOR
        MANAGER
        EMPLOYEE
        CUSTOMER
    }
    note right of UserRole
        One SPA for every role (Table 1).
        Guest is NOT a role: it is the absence
        of a session. Roles are consumed by
        WEB03 (navigation), never decided by WEB01.
    end note

    User "1" *-- "1" UserId : identified by >
    User "1" --> "0..*" UserRole : assigned >
}

package "Customer Aggregate" <<Rectangle>> {

    class Customer <<entity>> <<aggregateRoot>> {
    }

    class CustomerId <<vo>> {
        + value : string
    }
    note right of CustomerId
        Example: "CUST-00123".
    end note

    Customer "1" *-- "1" CustomerId : identified by >
}

package "Product Category Aggregate" <<Rectangle>> {

    class ProductCategory <<entity>> <<aggregateRoot>> {
    }

    class CategoryId <<vo>> {
        + value : string
    }
    note right of CategoryId
        Example: "CAT-00123".
    end note

    ProductCategory "1" *-- "1" CategoryId : identified by >
}

package "Product Aggregate" <<Rectangle>> {

    class Product <<entity>> <<aggregateRoot>> {
        + isActive : boolean
    }

    class ProductId <<vo>> {
        + value : string
    }
    note right of ProductId
        Example: "PROD-00123".
        Same value when referenced by the SPA,
        REST, forecasts and the Prolog knowledge base.
    end note

    Product "1" *-- "1" ProductId : identified by >
}

package "Stock Aggregate" <<Rectangle>> {

    class StockInformation <<entity>> <<aggregateRoot>> {
    }

    class StockId <<vo>> {
        + value : string
    }
    note right of StockId
        Example: "STOCK-00123".
    end note

    StockInformation "1" *-- "1" StockId : identified by >
}

Customer "0..1" --> "0..1" User : associated with >
Product "0..*" --> "1" ProductCategory : categorized by >
StockInformation "0..*" --> "1" Product : tracks stock periods for >

note as WEB01Note
    <b>What WEB01 requires from these aggregates</b>
    - Identifiers are generated ONLY by the back end and are
      opaque strings for the SPA: never generated, parsed,
      incremented or rewritten in the browser (BR 4).
    - Reuse the identifier for the same resource across
      components (AC 3). ProductId identifies a product;
      the viewer uses the active kitchen configuration's
      own identifier and asset references (WEB06 / VIS01).
    - Business data is read and maintained ONLY through the
      Back-End API (apiClient); it is not cached in browser
      storage (BR 5) and is re-read after a successful change (BR 14).
    <b>Note</b>
    - apiClient, ApiError, appConfig and the module slot are
      technical concepts of the SPA (frontend/src), not domain
      concepts, and are therefore not part of the domain model.
end note
WEB01Note .. ProductId

@enduml
